# The blanket ignore rules that used to live here are GONE on purpose.
#
# skills/dev-browser/scripts/ was three things at once — published backends, private
# per-client scratch, and private tools — so the only way to keep the private two out
# of this public repo was to ignore *.ts/*.sh/*.pl wholesale. That rule could not tell
# a backend from a scratch file, so it silently swallowed seven real command backends:
# they lived on disk, the dispatcher called them, and the public repo shipped without
# them for months. Nobody noticed, because an ignored file looks exactly like a
# committed one until someone clones.
#
# The fix is layout, not a smarter pattern. Scratch now lives in
# ~/claude-tmp/<slug>/dev-browser/ and private tools in ~/dev-browser-private/ — both
# outside every worktree, so nothing under skills/dev-browser/builtins/ needs hiding
# and everything there is tracked. .githooks/pre-commit refuses any staged path under
# the old scripts/ name and any builtin missing from ALLOWED_BUILTINS.

# Scratch probes & backups at the skill root
skills/dev-browser/mg-*.mjs
skills/dev-browser/*.bak2
skills/dev-browser/375/

# Session handoff file — local only, never committed
.claude-handoff.md
